-- title:
--   Vanishing cycles: (τ-1)V inside unipotent-fixed GL₂(𝔽_q)-translates
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\lambda\ne q$. Assume `LevelAutInputs q M'`, i.e. for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is an automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `IsLevelAutBar`, and `GL2Laws q M'`, i.e. a monoid homomorphism $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\to\operatorname{End}(\mathrm{Jac}(q,M'))$ agreeing with `slJac` on reductions of $\Gamma_0(M')$-matrices and with `diagJac` on the diagonal elements. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $P$, let $W$ be the finite set of supersingular places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ over the residue field of $P$, let $\pi\in P$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\iota:\mathbb{F}_{q^2}\to\mathrm{ResidueField}(P)$ be a ring homomorphism making the residue field an $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra, assume the Drinfeld coordinate ring over the residue field is a domain, assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the former along $P$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $P$ in the sense that any Laurent series over $P$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$'s ring of integers and has $R_0$-residue equal to its coefficientwise residue. Then for every semistable covering $\mathcal{C}$ for these data satisfying the nine clauses `EquivClauses`, `W2Clauses` (with parameters $\pi$, $\iota$ and $\eta=q$), `LevelPinClauses` (for the inclusion and $R_0$), `InertiaClause` at $\pi$, `WidthClause` at $\pi$, `GenusClause`, `DiscFibreClause`, `CurveClause` and `NaturalityClauses`, for every semistable model $M$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $P$ whose components are indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)\sqcup W$ through `sumFbar` and `sumChart`, whose annuli are the $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}(\ell,s)$ with source the component $\ell$ and target the component $s$ and node places given by `sumNode`, for every descent datum $D$ for $M$, and for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with `tameCharacter P π τ = 1`: the range of $\tau-1$ acting through `tateGal q M' lam` base-changed to $\mathbb{Q}_\lambda$ on $\mathbb{Q}_\lambda\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T_\lambda(\mathrm{Jac}(q,M'))$ is contained in the $\mathbb{Q}_\lambda$-span of the vectors $g\cdot v$ with $g\in GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ acting through `tateGL2` and $v$ fixed by all the unipotent elements $\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, $t\in\mathbb{Z}/q$.
--
--   This is the Picard–Lefschetz, or vanishing-cycles, input at $q$ for the full-level Jacobian: the toric part $(\tau-1)V$ of the semistable reduction over the tame extension generated by $\pi$ is controlled by $GL_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$-translates of vectors fixed by the upper unipotent subgroup. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_linearMap_tateProd_comp_baseChange_eq_and_eq_zero_of_semistableCovering_of_semistableModel_of_reduction_of_inertiaIgusa`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_linearMap_tateProd_comp_baseChange_eq_and_eq_zero_of_semistableCovering_of_semistableModel_of_reduction_of_inertiaIgusa), and through it the level-lowering step at $q$.
